            "vuln_file": "net/unix/af_unix.c",
            "stmt_text": "scm->fp = UNIXCB(skb).fp;",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This statement copies the file pointer from the sk_buff to the scm_cookie structure. In the context of Unix domain socket file descriptor passing, this creates a potential use-after-free vulnerability if the original UNIXCB(skb).fp is later freed while scm->fp still references it, or if there's a race condition where the same fp gets passed through multiple paths leading to double-free scenarios."
          },
          {
            "vuln_file": "net/unix/af_unix.c",
            "stmt_text": "unix_destroy_fpl(scm->fp);",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This destructor call operates on the file pointer list that was just assigned from UNIXCB(skb).fp. If scm->fp contains a reference that has already been freed or will be freed elsewhere, this creates a use-after-free vulnerability. Combined with the previous assignment, improper cleanup of file pointers during socket operations can lead to memory corruption."
          }
        ]
      }
